ainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147348#post1147348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyone knows if this rule should be followed by the pure too? In the Pure book 1st edition the rule is of course present.<br /> I think they sould follow it too. Even an men eater predator kings at armony 3 has his own human behaviour. Like hate everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hate and savagery a Predator King tries to emulate isn't born of human emotion, but of the disgust that Urfarah's actual Firstborn feels for the clever monkeys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T06:20:24-07:00","id":1147389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147348#post1147348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyone knows if this rule should be followed by the pure too? In the Pure book 1st edition the rule is of course present.<br /> I think they sould follow it too. Even an men eater predator kings at armony 3 has his own human behaviour. Like hate everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far I know that the Pure don't follow the Oath of the Moon, so I suspect the are sin free, it still affects their harmony by breaking it though, In game terms they still take breaking points but with less penalty than the forsaken. Though they take damage by touching silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 10-06-2017, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T07:43:18-07:00","id":1147409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147363#post1147363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hate and savagery a Predator King tries to emulate isn't born of human emotion, but of the disgust that Urfarah's actual Firstborn feels for the clever monkeys.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, sure, but it doesn't change the fact that they have actually an human emotional system, I mean, they live their ancestral hate and disgust through human feelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So far I know that the Pure don't follow the Oath of the Moon, so I suspect the are sin free, it still affects their harmony by breaking it though, In game terms they still take breaking points but with less penalty than the forsaken. Though they take damage by touching silver. </div> </div> </div>yea they follow the oath of the wolf in first edition, and the '' uratha shall cleave to the humans'' was present. Btw, I totally agree with what you said","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T07:51:54-07:00","id":1147415,"title":"","content":"They do seem more human-oriented this time around. At least most of them. It's easy to imagine the Predator Kings running militia-like compounds away from civilized areas, just like the Fire-Touched might have religious communes, seeking out humans gifted towards the spirit to add to their bloodlines. The Ivory Claws seem most likely to try to only mate with other werewolves, with their belief in the importance of bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T17:41:48-07:00","id":1147619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147389#post1147389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far I know that the Pure don't follow the Oath of the Moon, so I suspect the are sin free, it still affects their harmony by breaking it though, In game terms they still take breaking points but with less penalty than the forsaken. Though they take damage by touching silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>But even breaking Oath of Moon is only -2 Harmony Breaking Point ( I know, one of my players like to balance Harmony by this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). So what, by using Oaths of Wolf the Pure are only hit with -0 Breaking Points? It's almost non hit there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T22:32:10-07:00","id":1147673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147619#post1147619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But even breaking Oath of Moon is only -2 Harmony Breaking Point ( I know, one of my players like to balance Harmony by this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). So what, by using Oaths of Wolf the Pure are only hit with -0 Breaking Points? It's almost non hit there...</div> </div> </div> </div>Shame on him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (your player).<br /> Not -2 penalty like the forsaken but -1 while breaking the oath of the moon which is cumulative with the rule that you also gain -1 penalty per harmony above or under 5. so a forsaken with harmony 7 will have -4 penalty on resolve + composure when checking for a braking point, while a pure one would have -3.<br /> <br /> (-2 for oath breaking -2 for harmony 7 being 2 dots above 5, the same penalty would be for harmony 3.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T22:52:49-07:00","id":1147678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147673#post1147673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shame on him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (your player).<br /> Not -2 penalty like the forsaken but -1 while breaking the oath of the moon which is cumulative with the rule that you also gain -1 penalty per harmony above or under 5. so a forsaken with harmony 7 will have -4 penalty on resolve + composure when checking for a braking point, while a pure one would have -3.<br /> <br /> (-2 for oath breaking -2 for harmony 7 being 2 dots above 5, the same penalty would be for harmony 3.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The scaling penalty is directional; it's specifically there to make it easier to polarize to one end or another and harder to restabilize towards the middle. The Harmony 7 Forsaken would have a total -4 penalty for their Oathbreaking activities, but the Harmony 3 specimen would only be at -2 on the roll; their respective penalties would be reversed if they were instead killing a human packmate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:10:33-07:00","id":1147683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147678#post1147678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but the Harmony 3 specimen would only be at -2 on the roll; .</div> </div> </div> </div>The page 104 of the cor book states my claim, so no.<br /> Except if there is an errata out there I am not aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 10-07-2017, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:21:08-07:00","id":1147687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147683#post1147683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The page 104 of the cor book states my claim, so no.<br /> Except if there is an errata out there I am not aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>There in fact is a final download version of the corebook that fixed a number of errors with the text and layout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:50:37-07:00","id":1147695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147683#post1147683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The page 104 of the cor book states my claim, so no.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;When a character hits a breaking point towards Spirit, he subtracts one die from the roll for each point of Harmony below 5. If the roll fails, he loses a point of Harmony. When he hits a breaking point towards Flesh, he gets a penalty for each point of Harmony <u>above</u> 5. If the roll is a failure, the character gains a point of Harmony. This means an Uratha\u2019s Harmony can fluctuate wildly over the course of play.&quot;<br /> <br /> This paragraph is consistent between the pre- and post-errata PDFs of Werewolf 2e Core. Violating the Oath of the Moon is a breaking point toward Flesh and 3 is not a number above 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:22:21-07:00","id":1147705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147695#post1147695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This paragraph is consistent between the pre- and post-errata PDFs of Werewolf 2e Core. Violating the Oath of the Moon is a breaking point toward Flesh and 3 is not a number above 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the way this rule is written is probably flawed, the reason ?<br /> <br /> <u>Example</u><br /> <br /> A starting werewolf has harmony 7 but hey why stay there ? lets go to the cool 5 huraaaah!!<br /> I just have to sin unstoppably towards 5, oh I have no penalty on res + comp since I have to sin towards spirit, so thats difficult. but if I had a penalty because of my sin it would fall more easily.<br /> <br /> <b>Logical conclusion</b>: its difficult to lose harmony from 7 to 5 and it is higly unlikely to happen if the player is not intentionaly making bad things, like eating people.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the coin you need to violate spiritual stuff in order to rise from 3 to 5, also unlikely to happen, which means that a character once falling to a level of harmony he can go more easily upwards for harmony above 5 or downwards for harmony below 5, so in order to reach the desirable 5 you have to do nasty things in order to have a good chance, do you think that this is the intented design of harmony system?<br /> <br /> Now lets say you do have harmony 5 and by a bad unlucky roll you fall to 4, you need to do a bad thing towards flesh in ordr to have grater chance to rise.<br /> <br /> Don't missunderstand me, I believe that the system as it is its fine if you are willing to play the monster and do bad stuff, I don't think though that all pople would like to play that kind of game, which for me its awesome, but when you come to the point to violate the oath of the moon in order to achieve balance when you have 3-4 harmony, well that sounds somehow off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:25:59-07:00","id":1147706,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3773_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3773\" data-vbnamecard=\"3773\">Helur</a> , sorry sorry sorry I am totally blind not seeing this<br /> <br /> <b><i>Violating the Oath of the Moon. (Forsaken only, \u20132)</i></b><br /> <br /> The pure gain no breaking point for violating th oath of th moon .... ignore my previous statement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:30:55-07:00","id":1147708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147687#post1147687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There in fact is a final download version of the corebook that fixed a number of errors with the text and layout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where may I find the final version?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:41:52-07:00","id":1147711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147708#post1147708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where may I find the final version?</div> </div> </div> </div>DrivethruRPG.<br /> <br /> I assume Pure suffer similarly if they break their Oath to Urfarah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:49:22-07:00","id":1147712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147705#post1147705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the way this rule is written is probably flawed, the reason ?<br /> <br /> <u>Example</u><br /> <br /> A starting werewolf has harmony 7 but hey why stay there ? lets go to the cool 5 huraaaah!!<br /> I just have to sin unstoppably towards 5, oh I have no penalty on res + comp since I have to sin towards spirit, so thats difficult. but if I had a penalty because of my sin it would fall more easily.<br /> <br /> <b>Logical conclusion</b>: its difficult to lose harmony from 7 to 5 and it is higly unlikely to happen if the player is not intentionaly making bad things, like eating people.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the coin you need to violate spiritual stuff in order to rise from 3 to 5, also unlikely to happen, which means that a character once falling to a level of harmony he can go more easily upwards for harmony above 5 or downwards for harmony below 5, so in order to reach the desirable 5 you have to do nasty things in order to have a good chance, do you think that this is the intented design of harmony system?<br /> <br /> Now lets say you do have harmony 5 and by a bad unlucky roll you fall to 4, you need to do a bad thing towards flesh in ordr to have grater chance to rise.<br /> <br /> Don't missunderstand me, I believe that the system as it is its fine if you are willing to play the monster and do bad stuff, I don't think though that all pople would like to play that kind of game, which for me its awesome, but when you come to the point to violate the oath of the moon in order to achieve balance when you have 3-4 harmony, well that sounds somehow off.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Violating spiritual stuff&quot; at Harmony 3 is as easy as: having intercourse with a human; Staying a whole day out of the Shadow, or eating a hamburger. Not necessarily moral questionable things (to humans; to a venerable scion of the Hunt, is another matter altogether). Killing humans is also not morally questionable to werewolves, and &quot;eating people&quot; is both a spiritual and physical breaking point (so it'll skew you towards where you're most unbalanced), assuming you swore you wouldn't.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that Uratha morality concerns itself with one's word and a notion of personal honor rather than with concepts of &quot;right and wrong&quot;. Which is a flamboyant way to make a semantics argument, but still.<br /> <br /> Is it immoral to use silver against the Pure that came into your territory and tried to kidnap your children? Don't think many Forsaken would have a problem given that context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 10-07-2017, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:58:33-07:00","id":1147714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147711#post1147711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DrivethruRPG.<br /> <br /> I assume Pure suffer similarly if they break their Oath to Urfarah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> its for forsaken only","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T02:05:42-07:00","id":1147715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147705#post1147705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the way this rule is written is probably flawed, the reason ?<br /> <br /> <u>Example</u><br /> <br /> A starting werewolf has harmony 7 but hey why stay there ? lets go to the cool 5 huraaaah!!<br /> I just have to sin unstoppably towards 5, oh I have no penalty on res + comp since I have to sin towards spirit, so thats difficult. but if I had a penalty because of my sin it would fall more easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sheer number of rolls assures an eventual shift. That's part of the point of the Sacred Hunt countdown getting shorter as your potential Resolve + Composure pool gets bigger. That's not a flawed writing of the rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Logical conclusion</b>: its difficult to lose harmony from 7 to 5 and it is higly unlikely to happen if the player is not intentionaly making bad things, like eating people. </div> </div> </div>You're a descendent of the Great Hunter. Kill some dudes. Take a season off to live in the Shadow. Sever ties with your physical Touchstone so you haven't got another two dice to slow your fall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other side of the coin you need to violate spiritual stuff in order to rise from 3 to 5, also unlikely to happen, which means that a character once falling to a level of harmony he can go more easily upwards for harmony above 5 or downwards for harmony below 5, so in order to reach the desirable 5 you have to do nasty things in order to have a good chance, do you think that this is the intented design of harmony system? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Nasty things&quot; include &quot;spending time in or out of the Shadow.&quot; Changes in Harmony are allowed to come gradually and if your goal is remaining at the balance point then they probably <i>should</i> come gradually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now lets say you do have harmony 5 and by a bad unlucky roll you fall to 4, you need to do a bad thing towards flesh in ordr to have grater chance to rise. </div> </div> </div>Or take a break from ritual hunting for a while, or stay out of the Shadow for a goodly bit, or break out the silver next time the Pure come to town. Or hell, cut ties with your spiritual Touchstone if you're in a hurry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Don't missunderstand me, I believe that the system as it is its fine if you are willing to play the monster and do bad stuff, I don't think though that all pople would like to play that kind of game, which for me its awesome, but when you come to the point to violate the oath of the moon in order to achieve balance when you have 3-4 harmony, well that sounds somehow off.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Of course it sounds off \u2014 you're looking at the system as though an uphill climb ought to be managed in a handful of jumps without resembling extreme circumstances. A werewolf with the easiest time getting to Harmony 5 also has the easiest time falling out of it, so maintaining that balance for most characters is a thing they work on regularly.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T02:09:47-07:00","id":1147717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147712#post1147712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Violating spiritual stuff&quot; at Harmony 3 is as easy as: having intercourse with a human; Staying a whole day out of the Shadow, or eating a hamburger. Not necessarily moral questionable things (to humans; to a venerable scion of the Hunt, is another matter altogether). Killing humans is also not morally questionable to werewolves, and &quot;eating people&quot; is both a spiritual and physical breaking point (so it'll skew you towards where you're most unbalanced), assuming you swore you wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, eating people is only towards spirit, there are no sins that are for both, it is illogical and serves no purpose.<br /> <br /> What troubles me though is if the sins above 8 for flesh and below 3 for spirit are added to the already normal list or thet are just them and you ignore the orhers because you are already too degenerate and monstrous to care. I think they should add to the total rather than taking only them in consideration, so aharmony 3 dood should roll for both, mating with human and defiling a locus which makes sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T02:22:39-07:00","id":1147719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147717#post1147717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, eating people is only towards spirit, there are no sins that are for both, it is illogical and serves no purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>These aren't &quot;sins.&quot; They're breaking points. Eating people is both eating people and a violation of the Oath. That's two rolls in opposite directions, each with a separate chance to fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T02:39:31-07:00","id":1147720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147719#post1147719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These aren't &quot;sins.&quot; They're breaking points. Eating people is both eating people and a violation of the Oath. That's two rolls in opposite directions, each with a separate chance to fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they are both, and now you mentioned it what happens in that case ? you roll for both with their respective penalties?<br /> I mean that werewolf is the only game that yo make two rolls at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T04:11:43-07:00","id":1147725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147720#post1147720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually they are both, and now you mentioned it what happens in that case ? you roll for both with their respective penalties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I begin with the one I'm least skewed to.<br /> <br /> Re Oath of Urfarah: The corebook doesn't concerns itself with mechanics for Pure characters (not even their sacred hunt are described mechanically). There's still precedent for violating such a thing to carry spiritual ramifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 10-07-2017, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T04:39:30-07:00","id":1147728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147715#post1147715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> getting shorter as your potential Resolve + Composure pool gets bigger. That's not a flawed writing of the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> dood actually the higher your <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Resolve + Composure is, the easier is to succeed on breaking point rolls.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147715#post1147715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Nasty things&quot; include &quot;spending time in or out of the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> only that it poses no penalty on the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Resolve + Composure </span></span></span>roll in order to have good fail chance. dood you need to do bad things because only then you gain penalties in order to raise harmony closer to 5, and that sounds kind off, you know to kill werewolves and destroy loci in order to come .... closer to balance come oooonnn can't you see the obvious ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147715#post1147715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it sounds off \u2014 you're looking at the system as though an uphill climb ought to be managed in a handful of jumps without resembling extreme circumstances. A werewolf with the easiest time getting to Harmony 5 also has the easiest time falling out of it, so maintaining that balance for most characters is a thing they work on regularly.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>You are completely mistaken on this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T05:35:42-07:00","id":1147736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147728#post1147728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> dood actually the higher your Resolve + Composure is, the easier is to succeed on breaking point rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Therefore it is less likely to change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147728#post1147728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">only that it poses no penalty on the Resolve + Composure roll in order to have good fail chance. dood you need to do bad things because only then you gain penalties in order to raise harmony closer to 5, and that sounds kind off, you know to kill werewolves and destroy loci in order to come .... closer to balance come oooonnn can't you see the obvious ?</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'll still be rolling it over 30 times in a month if I hit Harmony 3, stick to the Gurihal and have a sexually active relationship. Penalties or not, my Harmony is bound to change. Once more, for the Nth time, these aren't sins. These are breaking points.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T06:16:28-07:00","id":1147743,"title":"","content":"While not listed in the Harmony section there are gifts and rituals that are breaking points towards spirit or flesh. I got a character that use plenty of those to force the change in harmony.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Gifts</u></b><ul><li>Full Moon 5 &quot;Crimson Spams&quot;: Dramatic failing it, breaking toward spirit.</li> <li>Nature\u00b4s Wisdom &quot;Beat Ride&quot;: Killing the animal you are riding cause the user to do breaking toward spirit.</li> <li>Technology\u00b4s Wisdom &quot;Iron Slave&quot;: Destroying the machine you are riding cause the user to do breaking toward spirit.</li> <li>Change\u00b4s Purity &quot;Father Form&quot;: Using it and not engaging in combat is a breaking toward flesh.</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Rites:</b></u><ul><li>Sacred hunt: Destroying and spirit or getting a gift by using it is a breaking point towards spirit.</li> <li>Totemic empowerment: Using it is a breaking point towards Spirit.</li> </ul><br /> Using hard leverage in a social situation is a breaking point towards flesh.....for some reason.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T06:28:16-07:00","id":1147745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147743#post1147743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using hard leverage in a social situation is a breaking point towards flesh.....for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly because you're trying to disregard the spiritual quid pro quo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T10:39:14-07:00","id":1147814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147743#post1147743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using hard leverage in a social situation is a breaking point towards flesh.....for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well because of using primal violence, tapping at your inermost violent beast nature to harm a being of flesh, it would have been a breaking point towards spirit if you used hard leverage on a spirit social roll.<br /> <br /> IMHO this breaking point should have been used only in case of torturing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T10:51:06-07:00","id":1147823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147728#post1147728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">dood actually the higher your Resolve + Composure is, the easier is to succeed on breaking point rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Your Harmony <i>doesn't change</i> on a successful roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> only that it poses no penalty on the Resolve + Composure roll in order to have good fail chance. </div> </div> </div>Again: Frequency of rolls does more for you than dice penalties will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> dood you need to do bad things because only then you gain penalties in order to raise harmony closer to 5, </div> </div> </div>I've had players roll more successes than their dicepool and I've had players fail on double-digit pools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and that sounds kind off, you know to kill werewolves and destroy loci in order to come .... closer to balance come oooonnn can't you see the obvious ? </div> </div> </div>&quot;The obvious&quot; here being that a Dog is a different sort of werewolf than a Fade and werewolves who aren't in a time crunch will generally manage to rebalance by avoiding breaking points toward the nearer end of their scale and load up on breaking points toward the middle regardless of the penalties involved.<br /> <br /> &quot;Defiling a locus&quot; isn't &quot;destroying a locus&quot; \u2014 it doesn't go into greater detail, but considering it's an unpenalized breaking point relating to a class of sacred space it's probably a fair bet that bringing competing Resonance into a locus in plain disregard for the Shadow is how that dip towards the Flesh is intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are completely mistaken on this. </div> </div> </div>It is my sincere hope that I do not have to explain why &quot;a Trait that changes by failing rolls is the most mobile when the dicepool to check whether or not it changes is very small and the mitigating bonuses are not present&quot; is the furthest thing from mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T10:55:46-07:00","id":1147826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147823#post1147823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had players roll more successes than their dicepool and I've had players fail on double-digit pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is always so embarrassing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a><br /> <br /> Basically the game presumes you'll be hitting these Breaking Points a lot, so you will be rolling a lot. This means that someone with a small dicepool is going to be flipping all over the place. While someone with a high one might be stuck in a Harmony they don't want to be in for longer periods of time. The cure for both of them (providing their goal is 5 Harmony) is more action which, in turn, means more Breaking Points. These are going to be split between things you have to do, for the story, pack, to repay debts with spirit gods and so forth, and things you want to do, to achieve a balance or enjoy some 'normalcy.'<br /> <br /> Throw these characters into a larger story and add the other dynamics of storytelling and you have more of a tense and unstable situation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-07-2017, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T11:51:02-07:00","id":1147839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147745#post1147745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mainly because you're trying to disregard the spiritual quid pro quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean i could see it because on one hand number of doors are very high for spirits and it would make sense for the breaking point to happen when forcing doors against spirits. But against humans it seems odd. Considering that a lot of things that you can do to humans wouldnt fly (harmony wise) against spirits and vice versa, its odd the fact of forcing a door would universally applicable to both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147814#post1147814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well because of using primal violence, tapping at your inermost violent beast nature to harm a being of flesh, it would have been a breaking point towards spirit if you used hard leverage on a spirit social roll.<br /> <br /> IMHO this breaking point should have been used only in case of torturing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that your personal interpretation on &quot;if using a hard leverage against spirits, that is a breaking point toward spirit&quot; or i miss a rule?<br /> <br /> As for the primal violence, it really depends. Forcing door covers a lot of other social situations beyond violence. From ultimatums to social threats.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T12:36:33-07:00","id":1147853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147084-the-uratha-shall-cleave-to-the-human-uratha-safal-thil-lu\u2019u?p=1147839#post1147839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that your personal interpretation on &quot;if using a hard leverage against spirits, that is a breaking point toward spirit&quot; or i miss a rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the same principal works in the social system with spirits, first impression, doors etc etc<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T06:23:33-07:00","id":1147984,"title":"","content":"Another in-setting reason might be that the human souls are needed to fuel the change.<br /> And to make sure werewolves don't waste their time (so to speak), some precautions were implanted to make sure they stayed re-productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T06:25:00-07:00","id":1147985,"title":"","content":"It is important to understand that not every action that causes a Breaking Point is necessarily &quot;wrong&quot; by either human or werewolf standards. There's nothing inherently immoral about staying out of the Hisil for a week, for example.<br /> <br /> It's also important to understand that werewolf, like most WoD games, deliberately makes you choose between your sense of self and what's socially acceptable. Just as a vampire has to face situations where she must either uphold her Humanity but appears weak and unreliable to her fellows or reap social credit and other temporal rewards but fall deeper into monstrosity, a werewolf has to face situations where she must either violate the Oath to uphold human ideals but earn the ire of others or uphold the ideals of her tribe but risk slipping ever further into the Spirit.<br /> <br /> e: it's not a coincidence that breaking towards Flesh requires you to at least remove yourself from werewolf culture for a while","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}